  "notes": "A compound verb formed from {飲|の}む (to drink) + {過|す}ぎる (to exceed). While it can apply to any beverage, it is most commonly used about alcohol. The pattern 〜{過|す}ぎる is productive and can attach to many verbs to mean \"too much\" (e.g., {食|た}べ{過|す}ぎる \"to eat too much\").\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{酒|さけ}を{飲|の}み{過|す}ぎる: to drink too much alcohol\n- {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎて{気持|きも}ち{悪|わる}い: feeling sick from drinking too much\n- {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎに{注意|ちゅうい}する: to be careful about overdrinking\n- {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎで{二日酔|ふつかよ}い: a hangover from drinking too much\n\nUSAGE:\nThis is an ichidan verb. The negative is {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎない, the past is {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎた, and the te-form is {飲|の}み{過|す}ぎて.",
